# Gold ICT Pro — Phase 9 Architecture Addendum v1.1

**Amends:** Phase 9 Architecture Specification, Phase 9 Implementation Charter, Pine Script Optimization Strategy, Phase 10 Compatibility Review.
**Type:** Refinement — no module boundaries change, no new trading logic added.

---

## 1. Immutability Model (replaces "append-only" ambiguity)

### 1.1 Rule

Every contract instance is **immutable from the moment it is emitted.** No module may ever mutate a field on an already-emitted instance — including status/mitigation fields. A state change is always a **new instance**, never an edit.

```
OrderBlock (baseId: OB-21, instanceId: OB-21-v1, status: Active)
        │
        │  price mitigates
        ▼
OrderBlock (baseId: OB-21, instanceId: OB-21-v2, status: Mitigated, supersedes: OB-21-v1)
```

This applies to every contract that carries a `status` or `mitigationState` field: `FVGContract`, `OrderBlockContract`, `BreakerBlockContract`, `LiquidityHierarchyContract` (`swept` transition), `MSSContract`, `POIRegistryContract`.

### 1.2 Revised Registry Entry Base Schema

Supersedes Implementation Charter Section 2:

```
{
  baseId: string,        // stable identity across the entity's lifetime
  instanceId: string,    // unique per emission (e.g. baseId + "-v" + n)
  supersedes: string | null,   // instanceId of the prior version, null if first emission
  type: string,
  sourceModule: string,
  createdAt: timestamp,
  status: string,
  integrity: bool,
  contractVersion: string
}
```

### 1.3 "Current state" lookup

Because history is never edited, any module or dashboard that needs "the current state of OB-21" must resolve it via a **current-pointer index**: a lightweight map of `baseId → latest instanceId`, maintained by the *owning* module only (e.g. Order Block Engine maintains the OB index, Breaker Block Engine maintains its own). This index is not itself a new contract — it is an internal lookup structure private to the owning module, rebuilt from the instance stream. Downstream consumers always read through this index rather than scanning full history for "the latest version."

### 1.4 Retention interaction (ties to Pine Script Optimization Strategy Section 2)

The bounded live-array retention window still applies, but now bounds **instance count**, not entity count. Superseded instances beyond the retention window are pruned from the live array; the full instance chain remains recoverable from the Institutional Event Log (which logs every emission, including supersessions), so nothing is lost — it's just not held in hot memory.

### 1.5 Impact on existing modules

No module's detection logic changes. This only changes *how a status change is expressed* — as a new emission rather than a field edit. Order Block Engine, FVG Engine, Breaker Block Engine, MSS Engine, and Liquidity Hierarchy Engine each need their internal state-transition code adjusted before Gate 1, since none has passed Gate 5 yet — zero cost to apply now.

