## 2. New Module 14: Engine Health Monitor

### 2.1 Responsibility

Report on the **engine's own operating health** — resource usage, not trading correctness. Entirely separate from Institutional Audit, which checks contract *correctness*; Engine Health Monitor checks contract *volume and cost*.

### 2.2 Why it exists

At 13 modules the cost is manageable; by Phase 11–12 with more modules and longer histories, resource exhaustion (drawing object caps, execution time budget, security call ceiling) becomes the more likely failure mode — and it fails silently in Pine unless something is watching for it. This module exists purely to make that visible before it becomes an outage.

### 2.3 Mechanism

Every module may optionally emit a lightweight `HealthPing` each time it runs:
```
{ moduleName, registryLiveCount, registryCap, executionTimeMs,
  drawingObjectsUsed, drawingObjectsCap, droppedCount, securityCallsUsed }
```
This is not a new architectural dependency — it's a passive telemetry emission, not a contract other trading modules read. Engine Health Monitor is the only consumer of `HealthPing` events.

### 2.4 Owned contract

`EngineHealthContract`
```
{ reportId, generatedAt,
  perModule: [{ moduleName, registryUsagePct, executionTimeMs,
                drawingUsagePct, droppedCount, overflowRisk: bool }],
  aggregate: { totalExecutionTimeMs, totalSecurityCalls, totalDrawingObjectsUsed },
  integrity }
```

### 2.5 Execution frequency

Periodic — same class as Institutional Audit and Statistics Engine (e.g. every N bars for resource snapshots; execution-time totals can be sampled every bar internally but only *reported* on the periodic cadence, to avoid the monitor itself becoming a cost problem).

### 2.6 Tier

**Tier 3 (freely evolving).** Purely observational, no trading impact, safe to extend with new metrics at any time without re-auditing any Tier 1 module.

### 2.7 Consumers

None — terminal, dashboard/reporting only, same class as Institutional Audit and Statistics Engine.

### 2.8 Updated execution order (supersedes Architecture Spec Section 5 / Charter Section 1)

```
1. MTF Structure Adapter
2. Liquidity Hierarchy Engine
3. Premium/Discount Array Engine
4. Fair Value Gap Engine
5. Order Block Engine
6. Market Structure Shift Engine
7. Breaker Block Engine
8. Institutional POI Aggregator
9. Confidence Scoring Engine
10. Trade Rating Engine
11. Institutional Event Log
12. Institutional Audit           (periodic)
13. Statistics Engine             (session/trade-close)
14. Engine Health Monitor         (periodic)   ← NEW
```

