## 3. Confidence Explainability

### 3.1 Rule

`ConfidenceScoreContract`'s existing `scoreBreakdown{}` field is upgraded from a loose debug field to a **formalized, structured factor list** — this is the explainability layer, and it is a Tier 1 mechanism (the *existence and shape* of factor reporting is frozen) even though the individual factor weights remain Tier 2 (reopenable, same as today's scoring weights).

### 3.2 Revised `ConfidenceScoreContract`

```
{
  recommendationId, poiId,
  score: number (0-100),
  factors: [
    { code: string, label: string, contribution: signed number, category: string }
  ],
  integrity, contractVersion
}
```

Example instance:
```
score: 91
factors: [
  { code: "CONF-001", label: "HTF Alignment",        contribution: +20, category: "structure" },
  { code: "CONF-002", label: "External Liquidity",   contribution: +15, category: "liquidity" },
  { code: "CONF-003", label: "Order Block Present",  contribution: +10, category: "poi" },
  { code: "CONF-004", label: "FVG Present",          contribution: +15, category: "poi" },
  { code: "CONF-005", label: "Discount Zone",        contribution: +12, category: "pd_array" },
  { code: "CONF-006", label: "Weak MSS",             contribution: -8,  category: "structure" },
  { code: "CONF-007", label: "Session Timing",       contribution: -3,  category: "session" }
]
```

### 3.3 Standard Factor Code Table (initial set — Tier 2, extensible)

| Code | Label | Category |
|---|---|---|
| CONF-001 | HTF Alignment | structure |
| CONF-002 | External Liquidity | liquidity |
| CONF-003 | Order Block Present | poi |
| CONF-004 | FVG Present | poi |
| CONF-005 | Discount/Premium Zone Alignment | pd_array |
| CONF-006 | MSS Strength/Weakness | structure |
| CONF-007 | Session Timing | session |
| CONF-008 | Breaker Block Present | poi |
| CONF-009 | Confluence Count (POI stacking) | poi |
| CONF-010 | Liquidity Tier (Major/Intermediate/Minor) | liquidity |

New codes may be added freely (Tier 2); the `factors[]` array shape itself may not be removed or restructured without a contract version bump (Tier 1 mechanism).

### 3.4 Trade Rating Engine — pass-through, not recomputation

`TradeRatingContract` does not recompute or duplicate the factor breakdown — it references it:
```
{ recommendationId, grade, score, confidenceScoreInstanceId, integrity, contractVersion }
```
`confidenceScoreInstanceId` lets any downstream consumer (dashboard, or a future LLM-based explanation layer) resolve the full factor breakdown from the Confidence Score instance without duplicating data — consistent with the single-source-of-truth rule.

### 3.5 Forward value

This is explicitly designed so that a future AI layer (e.g. an LLM call) can take `factors[]` as structured input and generate natural-language rationale ("this setup scored 91 primarily due to HTF alignment and a stacked FVG+OB confluence in a discount zone, offset by a weak MSS") without needing access to raw chart data — the factor list is a complete, self-contained explanation surface.

